From: WhaleOS <whaleos-dev@navercorp.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cros_gralloc_driver::allocate: fill zero plane stride/offset

Copyright (c) 2026 NAVER Corp.  All rights reserved.
SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
See files/LICENSE.wrapper in this ebuild directory for the full text.


After the per-plane loop that copies hnd->strides/offsets from
bo->meta via drv_bo_get_plane_stride/offset, the gbm_mesa backend
sometimes leaves these at zero for flexible YUV formats (NV12 et al.)
that it allocates by spoofing them onto an R8 1D buffer.  Camera HAL
clients reading the resulting handle then see y=cb=cr=0x0 on
lockYCbCr.

Recompute any zero stride from the resolved format + width and
recompute the offsets as the running cumulative plane size, exactly
the layout drv_bo_from_format() would have written.  Non-zero values
from the backend are kept as-is so backends that fill the fields
properly are unaffected.

drv_helpers.h is brought in under extern "C" because the helpers it
declares are plain C symbols (the file itself has no C++ guards).

--- a/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
+++ b/cros_gralloc/cros_gralloc_driver.cc
@@ -14,6 +14,9 @@
 #include <xf86drm.h>
 
 #include "../util.h"
+extern "C" {
+#include "../drv_helpers.h"
+}
 
 // Constants taken from pipe_loader_drm.c in Mesa
 
@@ -292,6 +295,30 @@
 		hnd->sizes[plane] = drv_bo_get_plane_size(bo, plane);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * WhaleOS fallback: some backends (notably the gbm_mesa one used by
+	 * Waydroid for flexible YUV formats spoofed onto an R8 1D allocation)
+	 * leave per-plane stride/offset at zero on bo->meta even though the
+	 * buffer is large enough to hold the planar layout.  Mapper@4.0 then
+	 * hands those zeros to lockYCbCr() callers and the camera HAL bails
+	 * out with "unsupported flexible yuv layout y 0x0 cb 0x0 ...".
+	 * If we detect a zero stride after the per-plane loop, recompute the
+	 * layout from the format + width.
+	 */
+	{
+		uint32_t cum_offset = 0;
+		for (size_t plane = 0; plane < num_planes; plane++) {
+			if (hnd->strides[plane] == 0) {
+				hnd->strides[plane] = drv_stride_from_format(
+				    resolved_format, descriptor->width, plane);
+				hnd->offsets[plane] = cum_offset;
+			}
+			cum_offset += drv_size_from_format(
+			    resolved_format, hnd->strides[plane], descriptor->height, plane);
+		}
+	}
+
+
 	hnd->reserved_region_size = descriptor->reserved_region_size;
 	if (hnd->reserved_region_size > 0) {
 		ret = create_reserved_region(descriptor->name, hnd->reserved_region_size);
